  "title": "Quadratic Inequalities & Graphical Regions",
  "content": "<p><strong>Quadratic inequalities:</strong> Factorise and sketch the parabola. The solution is where the curve is above/below the x-axis.</p><p>For \\(x^2 - 5x + 6 < 0\\): factorise as \\((x-2)(x-3) < 0\\). The curve is below the axis between the roots: \\(2 < x < 3\\).</p><p><strong>Regions:</strong> For \\(y > mx + c\\), the region is above the line. For \\(y < mx + c\\), below. Use dashed lines for strict inequalities, solid for \\(\\leq / \\geq\\).</p>",
